---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro"
import { releases } from "../data/releases"
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Installation — Neden"
  description="Download requirements, installation guidance, and first steps for Neden."
>
  <article class="site-container prose-page">
    <h1>
      A little setup.
      <br />A lot to discover.
    </h1>
    <p>
      Neden is in early development. Each platform’s download is published after
      its packaged build passes release checks. Read the release notes for known
      limitations.
    </p>
    {releases.map((platform) => (
      <section id={platform.id}>
        <h2>{platform.name}</h2>
        <p>
          {platform.requirement}. {platform.status}.
        </p>
        {platform.download && (
          <p>
            <a href={platform.download}>Download Neden for {platform.name}</a>
          </p>
        )}
        {platform.id === "macos" && (
          <>
            <p>
              Open the disk image, drag Neden to Applications, then eject the disk
              image. This preview is ad-hoc signed and has not been notarized by
              Apple, so macOS will warn on first launch.
            </p>
            <p>
              If you trust this download, follow Apple's{" "}
              <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102445">instructions for opening an unnotarized app</a>{" "}
              in System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security. Intel Macs are not
              included in this preview.
            </p>
          </>
        )}
        {platform.id === "windows" && (
          <>
            <p>
              Run the setup file. Neden installs for your Windows account without
              administrator access and can be removed through Installed apps.
              This preview is unsigned, so Windows may show a publisher warning.
            </p>
            <p>
              Embedded web content uses Microsoft's{" "}
              <a href="https://developer.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/webview2">
                WebView2 Runtime
              </a>. Install the Evergreen Runtime if it is missing on your PC.
              Hardware playback and system integration are still experimental.
            </p>
          </>
        )}
        {platform.id === "linux" && (
          <>
            <p>
              The Debian package targets Ubuntu 24.04 on x86-64. From the folder
              containing the download, install it with:
            </p>
            <pre><code>sudo apt install ./Neden-linux-x86_64-preview.deb</code></pre>
            <p>
              Open Neden from your application launcher. Remove it with{" "}
              <code>sudo apt remove neden</code>. Other distributions, Wayland,
              and hardware playback have not yet been validated.
            </p>
          </>
        )}
      </section>
    ))}
    <h2>Your first video</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Open a video from your computer.</li>
      <li>
        Load a primary subtitle track in the language you’re learning. Add a
        secondary track for translation if you have one.
      </li>
      <li>
        For definitions and explanations, configure an AI provider and your API
        key in Settings → Services.
      </li>
      <li>
        Click a word to look it up, or choose Explain line to pause and explore
        the whole sentence.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Build it yourself</h2>
    <p>
      The{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/HanifCarroll/Neden/blob/main/docs/desktop/INSTALLATION.md">
        desktop build guide
      </a>{" "}
      documents dependencies and current platform support. The{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/HanifCarroll/Neden/releases">release page</a>{" "}
      includes published builds and their notes.
    </p>
    <h2>IINA plugin</h2>
    <p>
      Already using IINA on a Mac? Follow the separate{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/HanifCarroll/Neden#iina-plugin">
        plugin instructions
      </a>{" "}
      in the repository.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
